gz-transport 15.1.0 (Jetty) + two zenoh fixes that are merged upstream but not
released for Jetty yet, cut down to stay ABI compatible with the gz-sim/gz-gui
10 binaries built against 15.1.0 (only src/ changes; no header or class layout).

1. gazebosim/gz-transport#966 (backport of #867, "Integrate Zenoh 1.8.0 - Part
   1/2"): queryables, subscribers and liveliness tokens are torn down on a
   detached thread, so undeclaring from inside their own callback no longer
   deadlocks. That deadlock hangs `gz sim -g` over zenoh (#741): the GUI
   unadvertises a service from inside that service's callback.
   Dropped from it: the std::enable_shared_from_this bases it adds to the
   handler classes (they change the class layout); the callbacks capture
   `this` as in 15.1.0. Upstream makes #966 ABI neutral in #968, which does not
   apply to gz-transport15.

2. gazebosim/gz-transport#965 (backport of #961): zenoh publishers deliver to
   other sessions only. Without it zenoh loops each message back into the
   publishing process synchronously, on the publishing thread; PX4's gz_bridge
   subscribes to the wheel/ESC command topic it publishes and takes the same
   non-recursive mutex in both places, so its rate_ctrl work queue deadlocks.

Not included: gz-transport#868 (Part 2/2), which fixes service replies that
never arrive: it changes public headers and inline request code compiled into
gz-sim. Node::Request can still wait forever; px4.Dockerfile bounds `gz service`.

Build and install: infra/build-gz-transport.sh

